# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# data/ first and for a reason: it holds 150,000+ archived snapshots and several
# gigabytes. Docker copies the whole context to the daemon before reading the
# Dockerfile, so without this line every image build would spend minutes shipping the
# archive nowhere — and the archive is the one irreplaceable thing in this repo.
data/

# Secrets. The images read configuration from the environment at run time.
.env
*/application-local.yml

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image anyway.
target/
*/target/
node_modules/
*/node_modules/
dist/
*/dist/

# History and tooling the build has no use for.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
scratchpad/
